    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "What is this place?",
        "lines": [
          "The Wealdmark. A big country on the back of something bigger. Nobody here has a title yet, you included.",
          "Heroes are not born. They answer the notice board. Walk, help people, explore, and the land starts to know your name."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "How do I get around?",
        "lines": [
          "Click the ground to walk. Scroll or press plus and minus to zoom, and M shows the whole map.",
          "Click a person to talk to them, or a tree, rock or pond to work it. Hold the mouse over anything and a small card tells you what it is."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "How does fighting work?",
        "lines": [
          "Click a monster to start a fight. It runs in real time. Each ability has a cooldown, shown as a sweep on the bar. Click an ability, click your target, and keep an eye on your health. Press X for auto.",
          "Your weapon sets your reach. Blades and daggers fight up close, a bow reaches six tiles and a staff five. If it goes badly you can flee, though the monsters stay angry for a moment."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "What is hit chance?",
        "lines": [
          "A weapon swing lands about three times in four against a foe your own level. A higher skill or accuracy gear improves it, and a tougher foe lowers it. It never falls below one in twenty.",
          "Spells never miss, unless something has blinded you. Open your stats with C to see your own number."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Skills, gear and bag",
        "lines": [
          "K opens your skills, where you spend a point each time you level. I is your bag, E is what you wear, and C shows your stats.",
          "Better gear comes from drops, from the smith, and from the shops. Rare and legendary pieces carry powers of their own."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Gathering and crafting",
        "lines": [
          "Chop trees, mine rock, fish the pond and snare rabbits. Pine is level one, birch ten, oak twenty and willow thirty. Dark-green narrow trees are pines, pale trunks are birch.",
          "Take what you gather to the smith and the cook. They turn it into gear and food."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Portals, checkpoints and signing out",
        "lines": [
          "Press T to cast the town portal. It takes a few breaths, you have to stand still, and it will not work in a fight. It carries you to your last checkpoint.",
          "Walk into a safe place near a bellstone or a town gate and it becomes your checkpoint. That is where you wake after a fall or a sign-out.",
          "One warning. Sign out in the middle of a fight inside a dungeon and you lose what that delve gave you."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Where should I start?",
        "lines": [
          "Take the kit I have for you first. Then Warden Osric, by the Tower north of here, has jobs for anyone willing to earn a name.",
          "Tam at the stable has imps chewing his harness, south of the gate. Clear three and you will have earned a hearing."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "quests"
      }
    ]
  },
